module sum_arg

// A SUM as a type ARGUMENT of a generic instance: `Vec[Sig]`. novac's mangler
// ices on this shape ("a SUM as an instance argument -- its in-name spelling is
// not measured on the shell") and its doc says the shape is unreachable -- yet
// novac's own sources reach it (`[]TokenKind` and kin), and that single ice is
// what pushes the self-distance runner into per-file mode. This probe exists to
// MEASURE the oracle's spelling of the instance struct, read off its C.
type Sig enum Off | On(int)

fn main() {
    ro xs = []Sig.of(Sig.Off, Sig.On(3))
    println(xs.len())
}
